 This skill owns the canonical template, the workflows that generate and refine ISAs, and the example library.
 
+**Invocation:** the Algorithm invokes this skill automatically at OBSERVE for any non-trivial task; it may also be invoked directly by the user to scaffold or audit an ISA outside an Algorithm run.
+
+**When NOT to use:** creating a new skill → use CreateSkill; running the Algorithm itself → the Algorithm invokes *this* skill, not the other way around; generating non-ISA artifacts → this skill owns the ISA primitive only; after-the-fact write-ups (postmortems, decision logs, engineering journals) → those are retrospective, whereas the ISA is a commitment-time scaffold for ideal state.
